//! The LOD system (`client/src/lod/lodSystem.ts`): each frame the octree is walked from the root
//! around the camera, refining a node while its cells project larger than the pixel error. A
//! parent stays drawn until all its children are ready (meshed, or known empty or buried); level-0
//! children are the streamed chunks. Unmodified sections are generated by the host's generator;
//! sections the LOD index says may be modified are asked of the server (LodRequest), and a
//! `Generated` answer covers the section's whole subtree. Jobs go coarsest first, then nearest;
//! content and meshes live in a cache bounded by the cache budget. Beyond the streamed view, the
//! chunks a refined level-1 section needs are asked of the server (ChunkRequest, within
//! RENDER_RADIUS_CHUNKS), nearest first. Distances are from the camera's position alone (not
//! ahead along its velocity).
//!
//! The collaborators are traits ([`LodHost`]): the generator ([`SectionSource`]), the mesher
//! ([`SectionMesher`]), the renderer ([`LodView`]), the streamed chunks ([`ChunkReadiness`]) and
//! the network ([`LodNetwork`]). A job is started with a token; the host reports its result with
//! [`LodSystem::on_lod_bounds`], [`LodSystem::on_generated`] or [`LodSystem::on_meshed`], and
//! results whose token is no longer current are ignored.

